Revision history for Web-VWF

0.003.0
	[ Enhancements ]
	- <display><directory> overrides the directory searched for page modules when no
	<page> is listed, and the page modules are loaded from it; a <directory> in a
	<page> says where that page's module is and beats the one in <display>.  A page
	with neither is found in @INC and the default is unchanged
	(../lib/Web/VWF/Display).
	- File-based caches (Berkeley DB, File) now go in $CACHEDIR, or failing that
	$CACHE_DIR, when either is set, ahead of $root_dir and the configuration; the
	directory is created if it does not exist.  Previously root_dir=example put
	CGI+3a+3aLingua, __db.* and the rest inside example/.
	- A data_modules entry with no :: in it is taken to be in Web::VWF::Data::, so
	<data_modules>index, states</data_modules> works; a full module name is still
	used as written.
	- The pages setting is renamed <display>, after the Web::VWF::Display
	directory.  The old <pages> is still read when there is no <display>.
	- The setting is now one <page> element for each page, with a <name>
	and a <description>; the description is shown in the 300 response.  The old
	string of names is still read.  example/conf/default uses the new form.
	- The example site has a states page (?page=states): a sample CSV database,
	example/data/states.csv (the 50 U.S. states), read through the new
	Web::VWF::Data::states and shown by Web::VWF::Display::states and the
	states.tmpl template.
	[ Bug Fixes ]
	- Handle captcha display failure

0.002.0	Wed Nov 11 08:54:17 PM EST 2026
	[ Enhancements ]
	- Added Web::VWF::Mail: sends mail through sendmail(1), signed with DKIM when
	the site configures DKIMSelector and DKIMKey.  Mail::DKIM is recommended,
	not required; without it, or without a key, mail is sent unsigned.
	Web::VWF::Display::index now sends through it.
	- Mail rejects a sender that could be read as a sendmail option or a header.
	- Declared the dependencies that were only loaded lazily and so were missing
	from the build files: Data::Validate::URI, DateTime, LWP::Simple::WithCache,
	Time::Duration::Parse, XML::LibXML and YAML.
	- Debug logging of the configuration now redacts secrets, keys and tokens
	(Web::VWF::Utils::redact_config).
	- Every module now carries the distribution's $VERSION.
	- Documented the API of new(), and of Web::VWF::Mail.
	- Corrected the README and POD, which described a site layout that is not in
	the distribution, and fixed 8-space indentation in two modules.
	- Declared the licence as GPL2 in the metadata, and kept example/ and t/ out
	of the CPAN index.

0.001.0	Tue Nov 10 09:00:49 PM EST 2026
	First draft
